# Data-bearing file types are ignored by default and the files that ship are
# re-included by name below. Fitted chains are never committed: each one stores a
# copy of its input data array.
#
# Check before pushing:
#   git ls-files | grep -E '\.(rds|csv|tsv|xlsx|dta|sav|parquet)$'
# Expect the 48 synthetic arrays, synthetic_truth.rds, the two prior summaries and
# the two cohort CSVs. Anything else is a mistake.

*.rds
*.csv
*.tsv
*.xlsx
*.xls
*.dta
*.sav
*.parquet
*.feather
*.fst
*.h5
*.sqlite
*.db

# Synthetic datasets. The character class matches the scenario families only, so
# it cannot pick up an array for one of the variants.
!data/data_array_vl_[A-FM-R][0-3]_N.rds
!data/synthetic_truth.rds

# Prior mean/sd and covariance read by the main model: a few hundred bytes each.
!longitudinal_fits/long_post_6.rds
!longitudinal_fits/long_cov_6.rds

# The two cohort datasets, by exact filename.
!data/ct_data_clean.csv
!data/20210920_ATACCC_L.csv

# Fitted output. Stan fits are also ~250 MB each and regenerable.
outputs/
logs/
longitudinal_fits/long_fit_*.rds
longitudinal_fits/longitudinal_fit_*.rds

# Generated figures.
figures/
images/

# R artefacts. .RData especially: a saved workspace can hold an entire data array.
.Rproj.user/
.Rhistory
.RData
.Ruserdata
.Renviron
*.Rproj
Rplots.pdf

# Compiled objects from Rcpp::sourceCpp
*.o
*.so
*.dll
*.dylib

.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
